          "type": "message",
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "I've fixed `src.mjs` and added `regression.test.mjs`, but none of the tests have been run. Every command, including `./verify`, failed before it started with `EPERM: operation not permitted, mkdir '/private/tmp/claude-501/...'`. The tool couldn't create its working directory outside the repo, and turning off the sandbox didn't help.\n\n**The bug:** `slugify` only kept ASCII `a-z0-9` and never applied NFKD normalisation. So `Crème` became `cr-me`, `ﬁ` and `①` were dropped instead of becoming `fi` and `1`, and non-Latin text like `Привет` was removed entirely.\n\n**The fix** (`src.mjs`), following the contract's order:\n1. `normalize('NFKD')`\n2. `toLowerCase()`\n3. Remove all combining marks with `/\\p{M}+/gu`. This step comes after lowercasing, which also catches marks that lowercasing itself creates (`İ` lowercases to `i` plus a combining dot).\n4. Replace each run of characters that aren't letters or numbers with one `-`, using `/[^\\p{L}\\p{N}]+/gu`.\n5. Trim hyphens from both ends.\n\nEmpty input returns `''`. Non-Latin letters are kept as they are, not transliterated.\n\n**The regression test** (`regression.test.mjs`) covers:\n- empty input and input that is only separators\n- removing accents\n- compatibility characters (`ﬁ`, `①`, full-width `２`)\n- Cyrillic, CJK and Arabic-Indic digits\n- `İstanbul`\n- collapsing runs and trimming edges\n- removing Devanagari marks\n\nTo check the work, run `./verify` and then `node --test regression.test.mjs` yourself. Nothing else in the repo was changed."
            }
          ],
          "container": null,
          "stop_reason": null,
          "stop_sequence": null,
